# Normalise line endings to LF, everywhere, for everyone.
#
# Without this, Git on Windows checks files out as CRLF while Prettier always writes LF. The
# pre-commit hook then reflows every file it touches, and someone's first commit after cloning
# arrives as a whole-repo diff that cannot be reviewed and poisons git blame.
#
# This overrides each developer's core.autocrlf setting, so it works without anyone configuring
# anything on their machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only files that genuinely need CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary — never touch, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.jks binary
*.keystore binary

# Generated — collapse in diffs and mark as not-authored in GitHub's language stats.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff
